OK:  ChrHack 2.1 has been uploaded to wuarchive as
/pub/MSDOS_UPLOADS/games/chrhac21.arj 

Fixes:
   Rogue Level is now readable.  However, it doesn't look very roguish (sp?)
       Most of the chars are the same.  Stairs and traps are the only
       different things about the rogue level.  (And the lack of color)
   Attempted to fix the runtime 006 error (which the Pascal manual explicitly
       says should NEVER happen).
   Included a sample nethack.cnf file for people who still have the 006
       problem
   Added the trap and stairs symbols to the graphics editor for the rogue lev.
   Program convert, which will change your 2.0 chrdata.dat font file into 2.1

Notes:  If you're upgrading from 2.0

    1) Copy all the stuff into a different directory.  Then copy over
       everything except chrdata.dat (the font file) and nethack.cnf (config
       file)
    2) Run convert (changes chrdata.dat to the new version)
    3) Run chredit (edit the two new rogue symbols.)
    4) Run install (update nethack.cnf file)
    5) Have fun!

BTW:  The default rogue symbols for the trap is a diamond and for stairs are
the Xi character (three horizontal lines, also means Defined in math)

Rumor has it that chrhac21 will be included in the Real official distrubition
of nethack 3.1.


